Thanks for the effort, but I'd suggest closing this PR. It introduces an anti-pattern that bypasses the intended architecture.

## The Problem

Hardcoding providers in `BUILTIN_PROVIDERS` bypasses models.dev where providers should be defined. This:
- Creates maintenance burden (every new provider needs an opencode PR)
- Duplicates data in two places
- Sets a precedent for others to copy this pattern

## The Correct Fix

Update [models.dev](https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev) instead. PRs already exist:
- [#1023](https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/pull/1023) - `alibaba-coding-plan` (global)
- [#1030](https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/pull/1030) - `alibaba-coding-plan-cn` (China)

These are clean, validated, and waiting for review.

